# PulseMetrics - local env template
# Copy to .env.local (values below are the hosted Fluxis project; safe to use as NEXT_PUBLIC_*).
# Never commit .env.local or the service role key.
# No Docker / no local Supabase stack / no Inbucket.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ppwenukxtigxyjfejrfc.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_bebNsAN-c8bpZZD1GhBVxQ_wUmAifFV

# Optional: absolute site origin for metadataBase / auth redirects (no trailing slash).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: Sentry error reporting (omit locally if unused). Public DSN only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>
# Optional source-map upload on CI/Vercel (never commit the token):
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=

# Optional: service role for admin/seed scripts only (server-side). Never expose to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Hosted Auth dashboard notes (Authentication → URL configuration):
# - Site URL: http://localhost:3000 (dev) and your production URL
# - Redirect URLs: http://localhost:3000/login, http://localhost:3000/auth/callback (and production equivalents)
# - Google OAuth: set NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED=1 after enabling the provider
#   in Supabase Auth + Google Cloud Console; otherwise the button opens /auth/setup-google.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED=0
# - Email confirmation uses a real inbox (hosted Auth SMTP / Supabase email). No Inbucket / Docker.

# Demo credentials (seeded on hosted project in P2):
# Email: demo@fluxislabs.com
# Password: fluxis-demo-2026

# E2E notes:
# - `npm run test:e2e` uses mock auth (PULSE_E2E_MOCK_AUTH=1) - no real session needed.
# - `npm run test:e2e:hosted` hits this hosted project via .env.local (real inbox for signup confirm).
# - Optional overrides for hosted suite: E2E_DEMO_EMAIL / E2E_DEMO_PASSWORD
# - Never set PULSE_E2E_MOCK_AUTH=1 for normal local product use.
#
# Optional GitHub Actions hosted e2e (workflow_dispatch only):
# - Variable: ENABLE_HOSTED_E2E=true
# - Secrets: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# - Optional secrets: E2E_DEMO_EMAIL, E2E_DEMO_PASSWORD
#
# Hosted Auth hardening (Supabase dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Email):
# - Enable "Leaked password protection" (HaveIBeenPwned) when going live.